From: XTU MUSA bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] qwen4_exp/amd: use conservative QSA partial stages on MUSA

Candidate patch against vLLM v0.32.0; NOT hardware-validated.
MUSA's Triton path is closer to ROCm; use one partial stage for correctness.
This does not change the CUDA path.

--- a/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/amd/ops/qsa.py
+++ b/vllm/models/qwen4_exp/amd/ops/qsa.py
@@ -879,7 +879,8 @@
         block_n, target_splits, partial_warps = 64, 1, 2
     # gfx942 and gfx950 have a 64 KiB LDS limit. One software-pipelining
     # stage keeps the wide TP4 tile within that shared-memory budget.
-    partial_stages = 1 if current_platform.is_rocm() else 2
+    is_musa = getattr(current_platform, "is_musa", lambda: False)()
+    partial_stages = 1 if (current_platform.is_rocm() or is_musa) else 2
 
     num_tiles = triton.cdiv(logical_indices.shape[1], block_n)
     # Avoid empty splits when the selection width is smaller than the profile.
